# Template for .private-terms -- copy to `.private-terms` and fill in.
#
# `scripts/check_public_safety.py` reads `.private-terms` and blocks any commit
# whose staged content matches one of these patterns. This repository is public,
# so anything identifying a private trading environment must never be committed
# -- including in code comments, test fixtures, and documentation.
#
# `.private-terms` is gitignored on purpose. Keep your real terms there, never
# in this example file, which IS tracked and public.
#
# Format: one Python regular expression per line. Blank lines and lines
# beginning with '#' are ignored.

# Names of the strategies you run against this plugin, and their log files.
# MyStrategyName[_A-Za-z0-9]*

# Account names from your Zorro account list.
# MyAccountName

# Absolute paths to your private log or data directories.
# MyBroker[\\/]+Log[\\/]+

# Wallet addresses that identify your accounts. These are public on-chain, but
# publishing them here links this repository to your trading account.
# 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
